{
  "dataset_title": "Hidden Data in Filesystems",
  "description": "Hidden data were embedded in APFS inode timestamp fields. Each inode contains four 8 byte timestamp values (creation, modification, change, access). The lower 32 bits store nanosecond-precision values but were repurposed to hold 4 byte fragments of hidden data. The structure stays valid, while payload is distributed across multiple inodes and timestamps.",
